                <head>188. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On September 3, 1969, Richard Moose of the National Security Council staff
                    commented on behalf of the National Security Council on several legislative
                    referrals from the Bureau of the Budget (BOB) in a memorandum to J.F.C. Hyde,
                    Assistant Director for Legislative Reference (BOB). With regard to the draft
                    Romanian Trade Act of 1969, Moose noted: “The President has decided that for
                    present he has sufficient latitude to pursue the goal of improved trade
                    relations with the countries of Eastern Europe without seeking any change in the
                    Export Control Act or further authority to extend MFN treatment.” (National
                    Archives, Nixon Presidential Materials, NSC Files, Box 703, Country
                    Files—Europe, Romania, Vol. III Jul 1970–Dec 1971)</p>
            </div>
